  "summary": "I'm a graduate from UNC Chapel Hill with a B.S. in Computer Science. I'm a very quick learner: I completed all of my B.S. requirements in 2 years after changing my major from music and look forward to continuing my education whether in the workforce or graduate school. I take pride in the quality of my work, but also in my charisma and communication; I understand effective communication with coworkers, bosses, and clients is crucial to a successful business.\n\nMost of my skills are in software engineering but I enjoy learning about computer security, digital systems, electric engineering and other things. I'm fluent in Java, C, Python, HTML5, js, Google App Script, JQuery, and SQL, but also know PHP, C++, Verilog, Haskell, MIPS Assembly, MatLab, Prolog, and some BASH. I have an eye for efficient code, and consider it a challenge to see how efficient I can create programs without losing track of the bigger picture at hand. I know I can excel in any position given the expectation of greatness and look forward to finding a creative position where I can showcase my talent.\n\nOutside of work my passion is music; I play a variety of instruments including piano, guitar, drum set, and other percussion instruments. I have recently been learning audio engineering in hopes of having a quality home studio one day.\n\nGo Heels!",
